\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\fs28 3. Core Technologies Behind Generative AI\par
\fs24 What are Transformers?\b0\fs22\par
Transformers are deep learning architectures introduced through the research paper "Attention Is All You Need" in 2017. They form the foundation of modern Generative AI models such as GPT, BERT, Gemini, Claude, and Llama.\par
Transformers use a mechanism called Self-Attention, which enables models to understand relationships between words and context within large pieces of text. This capability allows them to process data more efficiently and accurately than previous approaches such as Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs).\par
\par
\b\fs24 Advantages of Transformers\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b0\fs22 Better contextual understanding\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Faster training through parallel processing\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Scalability for large datasets\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Improved language generation capabilities\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Support for multimodal AI systems\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\fs24 What are Diffusion Models?\par
\b0\fs22 Diffusion models generate images by learning how to remove noise from random patterns. During training, noise is gradually added to images until they become completely random. The model then learns how to reverse this process and reconstruct meaningful images.\par
\par
\b\fs24 Diffusion Process\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b0\fs22 Start with an original image.\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Add noise gradually.\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Convert the image into random noise.\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Learn to reverse the process.\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Generate a new image from noise.\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Advantages of Diffusion Models\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}High-quality image generation\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}More stable training process\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Realistic image outputs\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Flexible customization capabilities\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\fs28 What are GANs (Generative Adversarial Networks)?\par
\b0\fs22 Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs) consist of two neural networks working against each other:\par
Generator: Creates synthetic content.\par
Discriminator: Determines whether the content is real or generated.\par
The Generator continuously improves based on feedback from the Discriminator, eventually producing highly realistic outputs.\par
